WEBVTT

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.580
Hmph, you've improved.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:05.020
They all seem to be in perfect condition.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:09.860
I'm sure they will fully demonstrate
their abilities in the mission,

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:14.060
or rather, battle that is about to start.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.910
It seems the time has come.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:35.390
<i>That's how it always starts...</i>
<i>under the azure sky</i>

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:42.290
<i>After making a vow,</i>
<i>I now set off</i>

00:01:55.170 --> 00:02:01.680
<i>Yeah, the desert glitters with a golden hue</i>
<i>(The wind is scorching)</i>

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:08.020
<i>I'm searching for a diamond flower</i>
<i>(I keep on wandering)</i>

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:14.360
<i>Now, for the first time in my life,</i>

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:20.700
<i>I live for someone else</i>

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:27.210
<i>There's something</i>
<i>I wanna protect</i>

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:33.210
<i>I'll never,</i>
<i>ever lose it again</i>

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.710
<i>Resound,</i>
<i>my heartbeat!</i>

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:46.710
<i>A heartbeat smaller and fragile,</i>
<i>but tougher than anyone's.</i>

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:03.270
"Cat Sets Sail"

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:17.020
All preparations have been made,
so please rest and relax today.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:22.020
And tomorrow morning,
we will set sail for Kraken Island.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.580
It's finally time, huh?

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.030
What's the matter? Is something...

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.030
Train!

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.710
What's the meaning of this?

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:44.050
Stop, Train!

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.340
Train!

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.260
What the!?

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:03.000
You're!

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.670
Ch- Chrono Numbers...

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:11.230
Yes, I'm No. X... Lin Shaolee.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.010
What's Chronos trying to do
by gathering sweepers?

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:23.020
Of course, the capture of Creed Diskenth.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:25.320
Capture, my foot! You want his death!

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:31.360
As you say, Creed Diskenth's death.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:34.520
Rather, the annihilation
of the Apostles of the Stars.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.360
Annihilation!?

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.040
I see...

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.040
The Apostles of the Stars
are a nuisance for Chronos.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.380
And for us sweepers,
they make good bounty.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:50.050
So, it'd be a waste if you
don't take advantage of us...

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:55.720
Our target is the same, so there should
be no problem in how it is accomplished.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:59.390
How like Chronos.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:03.330
They do anything to get what then want.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:04.990
You're right.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:08.660
However, Black Cat,
you can understand, can't you?

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.930
The reason why Chronos operates that way.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.670
The hell with this!!

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.740
Now that we know
Chronos was behind this,

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.010
let's just call this whole thing off!

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:27.020
That's right! We're not lapdogs for Chronos!

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:31.690
I don't quite care for this turn of events.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:36.650
Sweepers don't take orders from anyone.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:42.700
The ideal of Chronos is world peace.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:47.040
Can't you understand that mind-set?

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.710
Bullshit! It doesn't matter
if we understand it or not.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:52.370
We're not interested in Chronos' mind-set!!

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:53.380
He's right.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:56.070
Don't take us lightly.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.380
This is why you're sweepers...

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:00.320
What'd you say!?

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:01.940
Why you!

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.880
You bastard!

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:10.660
When things don't go your way,
you immediately resort to violence.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:15.660
So sweepers really are
just barbarians, huh?

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.000
What!?

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.330
River-<i>san</i>!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:24.010
Then, you're saying
that erasers aren't barbarians?

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:26.010
After all you're killers, aren't you?

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.010
You don't mince any words, do you?

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:33.020
Well fine... just remember this much.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:37.690
We cannot allow Creed Diskenth
free rein to do as he pleases

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:41.750
He will certainly lead the world
on the path to destruction.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:49.700
How is Creed's condition?

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:55.040
He is doing just fine. The fusion of
the <i>ki</i> energy of Tao and nanotechnology...

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:58.710
The molding of unused cells and
giving form to <i>ki</i> energy substances...

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:00.980
Everything is going well.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.650
When Creed awakens, tell him this...

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:10.990
Sweepers eager for a 3 billion bounty
will head there shortly.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.990
Sweepers? Humph!

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.320
Such fools!

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.660
You'd better not underestimate them.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:18.990
Black Cat is also among them.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:21.000
I see...

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:24.670
All right. Leave the sweepers to me.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:28.000
Just keep track of their movements.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.670
Understood.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.350
I can't stop laughing.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:47.560
That's because the sweepers
will be the prey

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:49.020
for the weapons that I have created!

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:54.700
...for the living weapons created
through the fusion of Tao and nanotech!

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.690
Right, Echidna?

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:02.640
You're going to take care of them
before Creed awakens, right?

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.640
Are you worried about Black Cat?

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:07.640
Well...

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:12.170
I just dislike cats
who are too mischievous.

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:34.340
No!

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:36.000
Can't you make an exception?

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:37.400
No way!

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:41.680
Why?

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:45.350
Everyone gets scared shitless
just from hearing the name Kraken Island.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:47.680
Why don't you offer money?

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.680
You think I have that kind of money?

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.690
I just thought I'd mention it, is all.

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:55.020
We're like that saying
"The poor have no money"!

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:57.030
There's no saying like that.

00:08:57.030 --> 00:09:01.300
Hey! Still can't rent a boat?

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:04.630
Shut up! Why are you coming with us
if you're always complaining!?

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:06.640
Can't help it!

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:10.230
The sweeper alliance
has practically disbanded.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.650
I'd feel sorry for you if you were gonna
go to Kraken Island by yourselves.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:20.980
So super-strong me will go with you!
Be grateful!

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:23.320
--Huh?
--Bad sense of direction, huh?

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:24.990
Yes, he's got a bad sense of direction.

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:28.660
Why, the last time, he got lost
and ended up walking along the sewer.

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:29.990
Don't say that!

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:33.660
Please take the boat out!

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:36.670
No matter how much you beg, no means no!

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:41.340
The currents around that island are fierce
and we can't get close to it. Understand?

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:45.710
Um... I'll give you my treasure!

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:52.680
Apologize... to the girl!

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:54.680
Wh- Who are you?

00:09:54.680 --> 00:10:00.020
A brave sweeper who's looking for a boat
to go to Kraken Island, just like that girl.

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:01.360
Right?

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:02.360
Oh?

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:03.690
What?

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:05.030
Are you hurt?

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:06.260
No.

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:10.030
Believe me.

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:14.040
That island is cursed.
Better not go near it.

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:16.100
Sorry, missy!

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:19.010
Cursed?

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:23.040
Dammit!

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.380
And he calls himself a seafaring man?
What a joke!

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.380
Just watch me...
even if I have to swim over, I'll...

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:30.390
Can you...

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:33.320
sail a boat?

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:42.060
In Chronos' eyes, we, sweepers,
are just small fries.

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:43.730
Yeah...

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:47.400
But that guy said it was
for peace, didn't he?

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:52.740
Yeah, but the peace they're talking about
is one that fulfills their own interest.

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:54.740
That's a falsehood villains often use!

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:58.080
I shoulda let 'im have it then!

00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:59.410
Damn right!

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:01.850
Next time I see him,
he won't get away so easily!

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:08.690
But I sorta understand what
that Shaolee guy was saying.

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:09.690
Huh?

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.030
I don't know much about Chronos,

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:16.030
but I think them trying to destroy
the Apostles of the Stars is a good thing.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:18.370
I'm not smart, so I can't explain it well,

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:23.200
but if everyone in the world
can live peacefully, or happily,

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:25.040
I think that's good.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:29.380
Mundock, are you... stupid!?

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:31.710
We, sweepers, aren't champions of justice!

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:35.380
We work for money!
In other words, this is business!

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:37.250
Business!

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:46.690
But none of us are here for the money...
I know that much...

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:53.740
This is a personal thing...

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:57.740
but I'm very interested in you.

00:11:57.740 --> 00:12:01.010
People even called you
the legendary eraser, Black Cat.

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:05.350
Why is someone like you working
as a mere sweeper?

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.680
That's none of your business.

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:10.020
Well, it is.

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:12.350
I've always thought...

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:16.690
that I'd become a member
of Chronos Numbers like you.

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:21.360
You, as an eraser, were indeed my goal,

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:23.030
and I really admired you.

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:36.040
How's this?

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.380
Err... well...

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:40.380
A box, an umbrella and tires.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:42.380
Eve, that's rude.

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:47.390
You don't expect to sail
to Kraken Island in that thing?!

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:49.720
Hey, cut it out!

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:56.260
Huh? Err... I didn't mean it
like that... Uhm...

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:01.340
Hey, this is a fine boat!

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:04.340
Awright! Off to Kraken Island we go now!

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:06.340
Row! Row!

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:08.640
It's impossible after all, isn't it?

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:13.350
H- Hey, where're you going?

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:16.020
I'm going to look for a bigger boat.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.650
Oh, I see...

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:28.630
Is it revenge? For Saya Minatsuki?

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:34.640
It didn't take long to find out
the circumstances surrounding No. XIII

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:37.300
up until the time he left Chronos.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:44.710
So there shouldn't be any problem.
Our target is the same.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:47.050
Why not join forces against
the Apostles of the Stars so that...

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:50.720
I already told you. I don't trust Chronos.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.390
Why not?

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:55.390
The sweeper alliance is a decoy, isn't it?

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:57.730
While the sweepers draw the attention
of the Apostles of the Stars...

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.730
the Numbers will attack their base...

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:03.530
I see... so you have it all figured out.

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:10.340
And you want to say that
that is a dirty trick?

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:13.680
However, failure is not
an option for Chronos.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:19.010
That is because our loss means
the destruction of the world order.

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:22.350
Hence, we cannot be picky
about our methods.

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:24.020
Err... missy...

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:28.020
I think you'd better go home soon
or your mommy and daddy will worry.

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:29.020
I don't have any.

00:14:29.020 --> 00:14:30.690
Huh?

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:32.820
I don't have a mommy or daddy.

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:36.030
Don't have...

00:14:36.030 --> 00:14:37.660
Oh!

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:44.370
Chronos bears a very heavy responsibility
on its shoulders.

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:48.040
It's much different from sweepers
who are merely bounty hunters.

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:50.380
Well, I'm a sweeper, too.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:54.380
No, you are of the
same caliber as the Numbers.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:56.380
Why don't you quit pretending
to be some lowly sweeper

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.390
and return to Chronos?

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:02.320
For someone like you, the elders
are sure to permit your return!

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:05.660
You don't understand anything.

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:08.660
I left Chronos because
I wanted to be a sweeper...

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:14.070
in order to gain the freedom to
think on my own and to live as I please.

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:18.340
I have no intention of returning now...
not one bit.

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:23.040
Freedom to you means turning your back
on justice and fighting for revenge?

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:27.680
I'll ask you one more time...
Train Heartnet!

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:31.020
You don't have any intention
of following Chronos' noble cause?

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:34.020
I'll settle with Creed myself.

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:37.030
And I won't allow Chronos to interfere.

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:39.030
I see...

00:15:39.030 --> 00:15:41.960
I guess I still couldn't get you to see...

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:47.370
A sweeper can never win against Chronos...

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:49.700
because the responsibility
we shoulder is much heavier.

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:51.370
I wonder about that.

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:57.140
A stray cat sweeper may be living
with a much heavier burden, you know.

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:00.980
Shall we see about that?

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:14.820
What the!?

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:22.000
What the hell are these things!?

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:26.140
Is this... no way!

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:31.170
Transformation!?

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.680
Ahhhh!

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:37.690
What's this!? It doesn't
look like it's just nanotech!

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:39.850
It's probably that "Tao" thing, isn't it!?

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:43.020
The fusion of nanotech and Tao!

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:46.090
So, this is the answer the
Apostles of the Stars were seeking!!

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:49.700
Damn you!

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:52.370
--Are you all right!?
--Monsters! Those monsters!

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:53.030
What!?

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:56.040
On Kraken Island, those monsters
took my mommy and daddy!

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:58.530
Then you were on Kraken Island!?

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:02.640
Daddy put the boat out and let me escape!

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:04.810
The island became full of monsters!

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:10.720
I see... Okay.

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:13.990
You stay put right here.

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:18.980
The sweepers will take care
of all the bad monsters!

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:21.790
Sweepers?

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:33.680
This way!

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:35.010
Are you all right?

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:36.600
Hurry and get away!

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:40.010
Let's go!

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:40.980
Yes!

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:43.750
It's useless!

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:52.650
What!?

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:03.970
What... what are you fighting for?

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:06.310
Huh?

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.640
Well, I'm a sweeper.

00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:12.480
So, I'm just clearing away things
that get in peoples' way.

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:17.540
Can you understand?

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.680
Train-<i>san...</i>

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:28.360
This is what sweepers are all about.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:37.000
Sweepers are fools.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.340
Even though it doesn't
bring in any money...

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:42.370
they're fighting for strangers...

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:47.500
And aren't you one of these fools?

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.620
Perhaps so.

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:11.640
If you want to use us as a decoy,
go right ahead.

00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:14.640
And we'll use Chronos.

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:16.980
That's fine by us...

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:19.640
I'm just glad you all came...

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:23.880
Mister!

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:28.320
What're you doing here?

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:31.330
Please... take me to the island!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:32.990
Nope.

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:35.660
There are lots of monsters.

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:37.460
Uhm...

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:44.670
Then Mommy and Daddy...

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:47.340
Your Mommy and Daddy?

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:51.680
They're there! Mommy and Daddy
are somewhere on that island!

00:19:51.680 --> 00:19:53.170
I know it!

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:02.720
Okay.

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:10.030
I'll take on that job!

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:13.370
Thank you, Mister!

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:15.300
Be careful!

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:31.850
Huh?

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:39.730
The fusion of nanotech and Tao?

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:42.200
This thing seems
way deeper than I thought.

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:50.740
Where'd Rins go?

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:52.070
She said she had work.

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:57.080
Oh... What a busy woman she is...
as usual...

00:20:57.080 --> 00:21:01.540
Although, there seems to be
another busy woman here...

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:10.360
You're... one of the Apostles of the Stars!

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:13.260
The world famous actress...

00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:17.930
Echidna Parass...

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:24.760
What's the big idea?

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:33.710
Anyone... anyone who tries to harm Creed...

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:36.380
will be eliminated.

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:37.680
That's...

00:21:44.390 --> 00:21:47.620
Geez, that woman!

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.970
Creed...

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:21.360
<i>Since your new black boots</i>
<i>caused a blister,</i>

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:28.370
<i>you rest your right foot</i>

00:22:28.370 --> 00:22:38.370
<i>We'll keep walking along</i>
<i>with our own rhythm, without rushing</i>

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:51.880
<i>Don't say anything</i>
<i>because we'll soon understand each other</i>

00:22:56.430 --> 00:23:06.430
<i>I'm just holding you now to keep you warm</i>

00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:20.680
<i>I'm completely wrapped around you, so...</i>

00:23:21.090 --> 00:23:31.090
<i>Quietly the powder-like snow</i>
<i>is building up...</i>

00:23:40.510 --> 00:23:42.370
"Next Episode"

00:23:42.370 --> 00:23:46.050
<i>Awright! We've made it to the base</i>
<i>of the Apostles of the Stars!</i>

00:23:46.050 --> 00:23:50.720
<i>Train, I heard you have complicated history</i>
<i>with the leader of the enemy.</i>

00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:53.050
<i>Okay then, you just leave everything to me!</i>

00:23:53.050 --> 00:23:57.390
<i>I'll restrain his underlings until you</i>
<i>attain your long-cherished goal!</i>

00:23:57.390 --> 00:24:02.460
<i>Why, if I swing my knuckles,</i>
<i>these guys will be easily...</i>

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:02.660
"Sprinting Cat"

00:24:02.660 --> 00:24:05.060
<i>Holy crap! They're strong!</i>
"Sprinting Cat"

00:24:05.060 --> 00:24:05.430
"Sprinting Cat"
